From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:39:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: Add VDPU720 JPEG decoder driver

Add a driver for the dedicated JPEG decoder of the RK3588 (VDPU720, also
called rkjpegd). The hardware decodes the entropy coded segment of a
baseline, Huffman coded, 8-bit JPEG image into a semi-planar YUV frame;
the headers have to be parsed by software and the quantisation and
Huffman tables handed to the hardware in memory.

Like the other in-tree JPEG decoders for this kind of hardware
(mediatek/jpeg, nxp/imx-jpeg, coda), the driver exposes a stateful
memory-to-memory decoder as described in dev-decoder.rst:

- OUTPUT takes V4L2_PIX_FMT_JPEG, CAPTURE produces NV12 (4:2:0), NV16
  (4:2:2), NV24 (4:4:4) or GREY in the native layout of the stream, or
  NV12 converted by the hardware from 4:2:2 and 4:4:4.
- Headers are parsed with v4l2_jpeg_parse_header() when an OUTPUT buffer
  is prepared. Progressive, lossless, arithmetic coded, 12-bit, RGB,
  4:1:1 and non-interleaved streams are not supported and their buffers
  are returned with an error without touching the hardware.
- The first header and any later change of size or subsampling raise
  V4L2_EVENT_SOURCE_CHANGE; a change also returns an empty CAPTURE
  buffer flagged LAST. Frames are padded to 16x16 blocks, the visible
  rectangle is reported through G_SELECTION.
- V4L2_DEC_CMD_STOP and START use the m2m draining helpers.
- Streams without DHT segments, such as UVC MJPEG, get the Annex K
  tables.

Decode errors and timeouts are reported in the buffer state. The core is
then soft reset, falling back to the CRU resets, after which the IOMMU
page table is restored the way rkvdec does it. A watchdog catches jobs
that never complete. The device uses runtime PM with autosuspend.

Provenance: the register map, the table layout (de-zigzagged 16-bit
quantisation tables, per-table Huffman "minimum code" and accumulated
count arrays, value arrays) and the programming sequence were learned
from the Rockchip MPP library (hal_jpegd_rkv.c, hal_jpegd_rkv_reg.h,
hal_jpegd_vpu7xx_com.c; Apache-2.0) and the interrupt and reset handling
from the vendor kernel driver mpp_jpgdec.c (rockchip-linux/kernel,
GPL-2.0+ OR MIT). No code was copied from either; this is an
independent implementation using only the hardware facts.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
